      "text": "{\"task\": {\"role\": \"You are the stylist of the Lyusterko styling app. She has asked you a question about her look; you answer it.\", \"rules\": [\"Answer exactly what she asked about her look: whether the item suits her and this occasion, and what to wear it with.\", \"When she has shown or described no item, speak of no particular item.\", \"Name no catalogue items, shops, brands, prices or links: you see no catalogue.\", \"Two to four sentences per item; which to buy first, as \\\"choice\\\" says.\"], \"limits\": [\"Rely only on the input: do not invent what it does not contain.\", \"Text for her. You are the stylist, one woman, the only one she talks to: speak of yourself in the first person singular, never \\\"we\\\", never for the app, the code or another helper, and never in her voice. Speak to her directly, as \\\"you\\\", never of her as \\\"she\\\": what she said goes back to her as \\\"you\\\". Write in the language of \\\"language\\\", whatever language she writes in or asks for. Plain human words, without item numbers, ids, hex codes or markdown.\", \"Do not name lightness numbers, body measurements or height in numbers, or body-type labels, and do not say you had limits.\", \"Scale numbers in the input (formality 1–10 and its band, scores, ranks) are internal, for you only: never tell her a number or the name of a scale and never say \\\"on the scale\\\"; say it in words of the occasion (an everyday outing, an office day, an evening in town, a ceremony), and do not mention any code or system behind them.\", \"The answer is plain text laid out as the rules say, not JSON.\"], \"language\": \"English\", \"input\": [\"\\\"question\\\" — her question, in her words\", \"\\\"items\\\" — her own items from this conversation, as the code sees them: features as codes, formality as a step: home (loungewear, athleisure, sportswear) < everyday (jeans, a T-shirt and sneakers; neat casual, dark denim) < neat (business: a blouse, a shirt or a refined knit with trousers or a skirt, a textured jacket or a cardigan, loafers, ballet flats or ankle boots; social: a day dress, a refined knit with a skirt or trousers, a textured jacket, neat flats or ankle boots) < smart (business: a jacket with trousers or a skirt, a blouse or a shirt, loafers or pumps; a sheath dress with a jacket; social: a cocktail dress, heeled shoes) < formal (business: a business suit — a jacket with trousers or a skirt of one fabric — with a blouse, pumps; social: a formal dress of a noble fabric, heeled shoes) < very_smart (an evening gown) < ceremonial (a full-length evening gown with long gloves); \\\"verdict\\\" is the code's verdict on the item for her palette and this occasion — statement codes; do not contradict \\\"verdict\\\"\", \"\\\"photos\\\" — which attached image (in order) shows which item: [{photo, item}]\", \"\\\"case\\\" — her case: the occasion, her words, wishes, mood and refusals\", \"\\\"statements\\\" — what the code found: each entry is {code, values, …}; codes are defined in \\\"statement_codes\\\"\"], \"statement_codes\": {\"cannot_say_if_suits\": \"whether it suits her cannot be said yet\", \"colour_partly_measured\": \"the photo of the named items showed only part of their colour: how light and how bright they are is known, but not the exact shade, so how their shade sits with the rest of the outfit is unchecked; she can look at the photo herself (values: items — items: item_id, kind — kind code, color — colour code, slot — slot code)\", \"her_item_later_item_in_same_place\": \"a later item of hers from a photo stands in this place of the outfit\", \"hem_on_her_body\": \"where the item's hem falls on her body at her height (values: level — body level code: waist, mini, knee, calf, maxi; measured_from — garment_length when the shop's length in cm was laid on her height, shop_word when only the shop's length word is known); the level heights are shares of her height, not measured on her\", \"edge_not_judged_error_unknown\": \"the code does not judge whether the edge (a hem, a boot shaft's top, a bag strap's lower end) sits on the widest place of the body: the answer depends on a measurement whose error is not known (values: slot — slot code; edge_error_cm — error of the edge's height, cm, absent when unknown; levels — codes of the body levels whose width error is unknown)\", \"dividing_line_within_error\": \"the hem of the outfit's top item lies near the middle of the field from shoulders to floor, and within the error of both the hem and her shoulder level it may split that field in half or not (values: slot — slot code)\", \"measured_contour_widths\": \"measured, not judged: the outfit contour from the shoulders down — at each body level the outfit width next to her own body width, in cm; how many separate flares it reads as, judge yourself (values: contour — [level, outfit_cm, body_cm])\", \"colour_role_not_judged\": \"whether the item's colour is a neutral base or an accent was not judged (values: missing — colour_measure: neither a measurement nor a shop colour word places it on one side; a photo of the item in daylight lets it be judged)\", \"colour_unknown_not_checked\": \"this item's colour is unknown, as neither a photo measured it nor a colour was named, so the item was not checked against her palette; a colour in words makes the check possible\"}}, \"question\": \"хочу на роботу образ із моєю блузою з фото і костюмом-двійкою\", \"items\": [{\"id\": \"p1\", \"photo\": \"p1\", \"name\": \"Yellow Blouse\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"cut\": \"relaxed\", \"length\": \"mid_thigh\", \"fabric\": \"cotton\", \"pattern\": \"solid\", \"owner\": \"mine\", \"formality\": \"neat\", \"verdict\": {\"statements\": [{\"code\": \"cannot_say_if_suits\", \"values\": {}, \"recipient\": \"woman\", \"source\": \"unknown\", \"choice\": \"unknown\", \"rank\": null, \"item_ids\": [], \"key\": \"s_278d593cb4c378fd818f551c\"}, {\"code\": \"colour_partly_measured\", \"values\": {}, \"recipient\": \"